[2026-07-31T06:46:30.084Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=84f292bd0e5f77c6f6d4440a0f2d1d52] Topic: Restyle mobile navigation menu for dark theme
[2026-07-31T06:46:30.084Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=84f292bd0e5f77c6f6d4440a0f2d1d52]   Trigger:   The mobile slide-out menu still used a light, white-based visual style that clashed with the rest of the site's new dark UI direction, so it needed to be redesigned to match.
[2026-07-31T06:46:30.084Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=84f292bd0e5f77c6f6d4440a0f2d1d52]   Response:  - Updated the hamburger toggle button in MobileMenu.jsx to use slate/cyan colors and a subtle border instead of light-mode slate-on-white styling, and switched the backdrop overlay to a dark, blurred black layer instead of a light misty overlay.
- Reworked the sliding menu panel itself to a deep dark glassmorphism look (dark translucent background with blur), restyled the navigation links wrapper and active-link state to use slate/cyan tones instead of white/indigo, and updated the section divider color.
- Restyled the login/register buttons, the signed-in user info card, dashboard/AI Generator links, and the logout button to use dark slate backgrounds with cyan/violet accents and red tones for the logout action; also fixed a mismatched active-state check on the AI Generator link that was incorrectly comparing against the profile path instead of the ai-generator path.
[2026-07-31T06:46:30.084Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=84f292bd0e5f77c6f6d4440a0f2d1d52]   Decisions: The menu was moved to a single fixed dark palette rather than keeping light-mode-first styling with dark-mode overrides, aligning it with the same slate/cyan direction already applied to the desktop navbar so the mobile and desktop experiences look consistent.
